      "text_or_setswana": "In Setswana, how you greet and say goodbye depends on how many people you are speaking to.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "Talking to one person, use Dumela, O tsogile jang? and O kae?. Talking to two or more people, use Dumelang, Le tsogile jang? and Le kae?.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 3,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "Address people politely with rra (to one man) or mma (to one woman); for more than one, use borra or bomma.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 4,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "When you part, the word depends on who is leaving and who is staying: the one staying says Tsamaya sentle (\"go well\") to the one leaving, and the one leaving says Sala sentle (\"stay well\") back.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 5,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "Robala sentle (\"sleep well\") is used at night instead of Tsamaya sentle or Sala sentle.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 6,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Dumela, rra.",
      "english": "Hello, sir."
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 7,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Dumelang, bomma.",
      "english": "Hello, ladies."
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 8,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "O tsogile jang? Ke tsogile sentle.",
      "english": "How did you wake up? I woke up well."
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 9,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Le kae? Re teng.",
      "english": "How are you (to several people)? We are fine."
    },
    {
      "unit": 1,
      "order": 10,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Tsamaya sentle. Sala sentle.",
      "english": "Go well. Stay well."
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "The start of a verb changes to match who is doing the action: ke (I), o (you, one person), o (she or he), re (we), lo (you, several people), ba (they).",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "With bua (speak): Ke bua Setswana. O bua Sekgoa. Re bua Setswana. Lo bua eng? Ba bua Setswana.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 3,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "With tswa (come from): Ke tswa kwa Gaborone. O tswa kae? Re tswa kwa Molepolole.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 4,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "With nna (be): Ke nna Kabelo. — I am Kabelo. The full pronoun can stand before it: Nna ke nna Kabelo.",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 5,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "To stress or contrast who is acting",
      "english": "put the pronoun first: Nna ke bua Sekgoa. Wena o bua Setswana. Bona ba bua Setswana."
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 6,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "le joins two things: Setswana le Sekgoa (Setswana and English). kwa marks a place: kwa Gaborone (in Gaborone / from Gaborone).",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 7,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "leina (name) is a class 5 noun; its plural is maina. leina la me = my name; leina la gago = your name. mang asks who: Leina la gago ke mang?",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "text_or_setswana": "Survival phrases for now, explained in later units: Ga ke tlhaloganye (I don't understand), Bua ka bonya tswee-tswee (speak slowly, please), Ke eng ka Setswana? (what is it in Setswana?).",
      "english": null
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 9,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Ke nna Kabelo.",
      "english": "I am Kabelo."
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 10,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "O tswa kae? Ke tswa kwa Francistown.",
      "english": "Where are you from? I come from Francistown."
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 11,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Leina la me ke Neo. Leina la gago ke mang?",
      "english": "My name is Neo. What is your name?"
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 12,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Nna ke bua Setswana le Sekgoa.",
      "english": "I speak Setswana and English."
    },
    {
      "unit": 2,
      "order": 13,
      "type": "example",
      "text_or_setswana": "Ga ke tlhaloganye. Bua ka bonya tswee-tswee.",
      "english": "I don't understand. Speak slowly, please."
    }
  ],
